WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
Boston, Lincolnshire: a
market town in the fens,

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.250
home to about 70,500 people.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.310
Between the 2011 and 2021
censuses, it grew 9.1 per cent.

4
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.270
England grew 6.6 per cent.

5
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.730
About 4,000 residents
were born in Lithuania.

6
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.790
Another 5.4 per cent were born in Poland.

7
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.280
Yet 94.7 per cent describe
their ethnic group as White.

8
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.390
So why choose a small
fenland town over a big city?

9
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.470
Cheaper housing?

10
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.910
A quieter life?

11
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.250
In this mission, you'll compare
diversity between places and within them,

12
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.190
from Boston to London.

13
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.550
Then you'll test four explanations
for why diversity varies.

14
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.930
Your mission: explain why migrants chose
a fenland market town over a big city.
